BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Flying In
DTSTART:20250606T011500Z
DTEND:20250606T023500Z
DTSTAMP:20250606T011500Z
UID:XtIyi8npKt
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 60 mins (1h00m)\n\nPresented by Elliott Bay Book Co
 mpany. McGowan relays her often humorous and absurd stories in "Flying In:
  My Adventures in Filmmaking." This is a story told from the inside out\, 
 showcasing the perspective of a woman who started with no connections\, be
 at the odds\, and rose to produce international hit films.\n\nhttps://www.
 siff.net/cinema/in-theaters/flying-in
LOCATION:SIFF Film Center\, 305 Harrison Street
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:My Top 10 Favorite SIFF Films of All Time
DTSTART:20250607T010000Z
DTEND:20250607T025000Z
DTSTAMP:20250607T010000Z
UID:Bwe4cEE53H
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 90 mins (1h30m)\n\nThe Seattle International Film Fe
 stival has been screening films for over 50 years! In that half century\, 
 we have laughed\, cried\, cowered in fear\, and shaken our heads in bewild
 erment to thousands of films from across the world. Like many of you\, the
 se films tend to leave a lasting impact on our lives and influence the way
  we see the world. In this free\, members-only Film Talk\, join SIFF Senio
 r Programmer\, Dan Doody as he examines his top ten favorite Seattle Inter
 national Film Festival films that he has ever seen (excluding Secret Fest 
 of course). To reserve your free member tickets\, click the "SIGN IN" butt
 on in the upper corner of this screen. Once signed in\, click the showtime
  below to reserve your tickets.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/programs-and-event
 s/members-only-top-10-seattle-international-film-festival-movies-of-all-ti
 me
LOCATION:SIFF Film Center\, 305 Harrison Street
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Swamp Dogg Gets His Pool Painted
DTSTART:20250608T223000Z
DTEND:20250609T003000Z
DTSTAMP:20250608T223000Z
UID:qcfX9sXPxu
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 98 mins (1h38m)\n\nSwamp Dogg Gets His Pool Painted 
 is a wildly entertaining and fittingly unconventional documentary about co
 nvention-defying singer\, songwriter and record producer Jerry Williams\, 
 aka Swamp Dogg\, one of the great cult figures of 20th-century American mu
 sic whose singular voice and ideas have shaped the history not merely of s
 oul music\, but of country\, hip-hop and a dozen other genres.\n\nhttps://
 www.siff.net/cinema/in-theaters/swamp-dogg
LOCATION:SIFF Film Center\, 305 Harrison Street
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Neurocinema
DTSTART:20250609T013000Z
DTEND:20250609T035000Z
DTSTAMP:20250609T013000Z
UID:dIW4kfjqWC
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 120 mins (2h00m)\n\nWith films spanning experimental
 \, documentary\, and narrative styles\, NeuroCinema explores themes of ide
 ntity\, memory\, perception\, and sensory processing\, offering personal a
 nd nuanced perspectives on the lived experiences of neurodiverse individua
 ls. Tickets: $20 | $17 Member\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/cinema/in-theaters/
 grrl-haus-​neurocinema
LOCATION:SIFF Film Center\, 305 Harrison Street
END:VEVENT
